      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\), we will evaluate each term separately.\n\n**Step 1: Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil\\)**\n\nFirst, we find the square root of \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\nNext, we apply the ceiling function to \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\):\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\frac{3}{2}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil 1.5 \\right\\rceil = 2\n\\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil = 2\\).\n\n**Step 2: Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil\\)**\n\nWe already know that:\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n\\]\nApplying the ceiling function to 2.25, we get:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil 2.25 \\right\\rceil = 3\n\\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil = 3\\).\n\n**Step 3: Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\)**\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\):\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) = \\frac{81}{16}\n\\]\nNext, we find the square root of \\(\\frac{81}{16}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{81}{16}} = \\frac{9}{4}\n\\]\nNow, we apply the ceiling function to \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil = 3\n\\]\nSo, \\(\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 3\\).\n\n**Step 4: Sum the results**\n\nFinally, we add the results of the three ceiling evaluations:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 3 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
