      "text": "First, let's start by calculating each of the terms inside the ceiling function separately.\n\n1. Evaluate the square root term:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\sqrt{2.25} = 1.5\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 1.5 is 2.\n\n2. Evaluate the second term:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 2.25 is 3.\n\n3. Evaluate the third term:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{81}{16} = 5.0625\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 5.0625 is 6.\n\nNow, we will sum these ceiling values:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify the final answer using Python code to ensure the accuracy of our solution.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate each term\nsqrt_term = math.sqrt(9 / 4)\nceil_sqrt_term = math.ceil(sqrt_term)\n\nterm_2 = 9 / 4\nceil_term_2 = math.ceil(term_2)\n\nterm_3 = (9 / 4) ** 2\nceil_term_3 = math.ceil(term_3)\n\n# Sum the ceiling values\nfinal_answer = ceil_sqrt_term + ceil_term_2 + ceil_term_3\nprint(final_answer)\n```",
